  "evidencia": "Page: Macworld. Sentence: Macworld is a web site dedicated to products and software of Apple Inc., published by Mac Publishing, which is headquartered in San Francisco, California.\nPage: Macworld. Sentence: It started life as a print magazine in 1984 and had the largest audited circulation (both total and newsstand) of Macintosh-focused magazines in North America, more than double its nearest competitor, \"MacLife\" (formerly \"MacAddict\").\nPage: Macworld. Sentence: \"Macworld\" was founded by David Bunnell (publisher) and Andrew Fluegelman (editor).\nPage: Soaps In Depth. Sentence: Soaps In Depth is a series of magazines created in 1997 by Bauer Publications to give American soap opera viewers more variety in their soap-related magazine purchases.\nPage: Chris Breen (editor). Sentence: He was a senior editor at Mac Publishing, a division of International Data Group which publishes the US edition of \"Macworld\".",
