        "original_id": "500ab563-86f8-557b-8dfa-6257f34f3a3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Macworld, Mac Publishing, Apple Inc., International Data Group, Bauer Publications\n- People: David Bunnell, Andrew Fluegelman, Chris Breen\n- Places: San Francisco, California, North America\n- Products: MacLife, MacAddict, Soaps In Depth\n- Topics: print magazines, web sites, Macintosh-focused magazines, soap opera magazines\n\nFacts:\n- Macworld started as a print magazine in 1984.\n- David Bunnell founded Macworld as publisher, and Andrew Fluegelman founded Macworld as editor.\n- Macworld had the largest audited total and newsstand circulation among Macintosh-focused magazines in North America, at more than double the circulation of its nearest competitor, MacLife, formerly called MacAddict.\n- Soaps In Depth was created in 1997 by Bauer Publications to give American soap opera viewers more variety in soap-related magazine purchases.\n- Macworld is a web site dedicated to Apple Inc. products and software.\n- Macworld is published by Mac Publishing, which is headquartered in San Francisco, California.\n- Chris Breen was a senior editor at Mac Publishing.\n- Mac Publishing is a division of International Data Group, which publishes the U.S. edition of Macworld.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
